        <h1>LeetCode 2029: Stone Game IX (C++)</h1>
        <div class="problem-description">
            <p><strong>Problem:</strong>
                Alice and Bob play a game with a row of stones, each having a value. Players alternately remove a stone,
                and the running total of removed stone values must never be divisible by 3 right after a player's turn,
                otherwise that player loses. Alice goes first. Return true if Alice can win, assuming both play
                optimally.
            </p>
            <p><strong>Example:</strong>
                Input: stones = [2,1]<br>
                Output: true<br>
                Explanation: Alice removes a stone first; regardless of which one she picks, the running sum after her
                move is not divisible by 3, and she can force Bob into a losing position on his subsequent turns.
            </p>
        </div>
        <div class="code-container">
            <button class="copy-button" onclick="copyCode(this)">Copy Code</button>
            <pre><code class="language-cpp">class Solution {
public:
    bool stoneGameIX(vector&lt;int&gt;&amp; stones) {
        int freq[3] = {0, 0, 0};
        for (int value : stones) {
            freq[value % 3]++;
        }
        if (freq[0] % 2 == 0) {
            return freq[1] &gt; 0 &amp;&amp; freq[2] &gt; 0;
        }
        return abs(freq[1] - freq[2]) &gt; 2;
    }
};</code></pre>
